Which context for "it" is important here - Dragon scales, dragon
mail, leather, studded leather and massively heavy crystal armor
types do not interfere with spells.  The various metal armor
types do interfere with spells.  So if "it" here means body armor
in general then it depends.  If "it" here means dragon armor, no.

> > So, I ask for advice. My monk
> > (XP:16, AC:-32, somewhere in Gehennom) has a set of black dragon
> > scales. Is it worth wearing these (and/or fixing them into mail) for
> > the extra AC?
>
> -32 AC is very ascendable, but -45 would be even nicer.  So yes.  You'll
> need to max your Luck, if you haven't already.  You might want to gain a
> few XLs, too.
>
> G/S DSM is a better choice.

BDSM gives very good extra AC points plus disintegration
resistance.  Having eaten the corpse you already have
disintegration resistance.  It's one of those condundrums of
black dragon armor that it gives you an extra that you already
have.  But you can't get the benefits of gray or silver dragon
armor from eating those corpses and that makes those
specific types of dragon armor the best.

Is it worth the hassle in combat for the extra AC points?  I
can't answer that for you but it does boil down to that question
in your current situation.



